<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ardaric</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 450s</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ardaric was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a> in the mid 5th century and, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jordanes">Jordanes</a>, one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>'s most trusted subject rulers. After Attila's death in 453 he led the revolt of the subject peoples against his sons and won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nedao">Battle of Nedao</a> in 454. The victory broke the Hunnic empire and let the Gepids take over the lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>.</p></div>
